    "created_at": "2017-03-14T04:10:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-03-14T04:11:01Z",
    "body": "There's a bit of issue with the markup itself. The HTML parser would automatically yank the second and the third `li` elements out of the outer `li` because nested `li` isn't allowed by the parser unless there is a [special](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#special) element between them.\r\n\r\nSee the section [\"A start tag whose tag name is 'li'\"](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#parsing-main-inbody)\r\n\r\nI don't know how you'd fix this short of modifying the parser itself.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/286317012/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
      "+1": 0,
      "-1": 0,
      "laugh": 0,
