    "created_at": "2017-03-14T15:06:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-03-14T15:06:17Z",
    "body": "> There's a bit of issue with the markup itself. ... I don't know how you'd fix this short of modifying the parser itself.\r\n\r\nThat's a good point. (Here's a quick repro that makes it easy to visually see: http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/?saved=4944 .) So in this example `<my-list>` has no `<li>` children at all to put into the slot. As @annevk said we'd need template-like parsing for custom elements for this to work.\r\n\r\nGiven that I am now less optimistic about fixing this, since we decided against such parsing in https://github.com/w3c/webcomponents/issues/59 (which despite its title eventually extended to both slot and template).\r\n\r\nI guess `<template is=\"my-list\">` could still work for this use case.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
