    "created_at": "2017-03-14T22:32:51Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-03-14T22:33:23Z",
    "body": "Yes, using `<li>` start tag without a corresponding closing tag is extremely common on the Web.\r\n\r\nI agree with @domenic that fixing this won't be useful / possible without modifying the parser. I'm open to the idea of adding special token or special parser behavior in a limited case to address that though since the HTML parser seems to be causing a lot of pains for custom element use cases.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
