    "created_at": "2017-03-15T04:00:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-03-15T04:03:19Z",
    "body": "Oh, no, that's a feature; we use it within most WHATWG specs in fact. The Google style guide even mandates it.  Tag omission (not just `<li>`, but `<p>` and many others) is part of what makes HTML good and useful and more successful than XHTML!\r\n\r\nWe have no intention of ever removing or changing such a useful feature.\r\n\r\n(Another example: the Google HTML style guide used to explicitly recommend it, and now doesn't do that but does give an example of best practices that omits end tags.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
